A booking service checks for overlaps and then inserts:
```sql
BEGIN;
SELECT 1 FROM bookings
 WHERE room=4 AND slot='09:00'
 FOR UPDATE;
-- No returned row means no row lock.
-- The application then inserts:
INSERT INTO bookings(room,slot)
 VALUES (4,'09:00');
COMMIT;
```
Under Read Committed, two requests run at once and double-book. Why didn't `FOR UPDATE` help?
